{"links":[{"id":"5db81df9b9f0","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_act","w":"chrysostomus.hom_act","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":33,"p":[1,1],"r":[1,1],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Edd. epixwriazein , Cat. egxronizein , substituted for the less usual egxwriazein of A. b.c. Sav.-Below, Sumewn, fhsin, echghsato en tw Louka profhteusaj . Cat. \"He who in Luke prophesied, Lord, now lettest Thou Thy servant depart.\"-It is remarkable that it does not occur to Chrys. that Symeon is Simon Peter, though 2 Pet. i. 1 has Sumewn Petroj in the Cod. Alexandr., and many other mss. In the Mod. text Chrys. is made to say: \"Some say that this is he who is mentioned by Luke: others, that he is some other person of the same name. (Acts xiii. 1?) But whether it be the one or the other is a point about which there is no need to be particular; but only. to receive as necessary the things which the person declared.\""},{"id":"e521736f6bc6","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_rom","w":"chrysostomus.hom_rom","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":14,"p":[13,13],"r":[3,13],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"2 Pet. iii. 13"},{"id":"9e915b81b578","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_rom","w":"chrysostomus.hom_rom","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":25,"p":[19,19],"r":[2,14],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"See Matt. v. 28, and 2 Pet. ii. 14. And with respect to giving cause of offence to others, Mark. ix. 44."},{"id":"18410e65fae8","v":"npnf.ambrosius.de_spiritu_sancto","w":"ambrosius.de_spiritu_sancto","a":"ambrosius_von_mailand","s":5,"p":[1,1],"r":[1,21],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"2 Pet. i. 21."},{"id":"0726df47136d","v":"npnf.augustinus.de_civitate_dei","w":"augustinus.de_civitate_dei","a":"augustinus_von_hippo","s":333,"p":[0,0],"r":[2,4],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"2 Peter ii. 4."},{"id":"09ef722669f3","v":"npnf.augustinus.de_civitate_dei","w":"augustinus.de_civitate_dei","a":"augustinus_von_hippo","s":534,"p":[0,0],"r":[2,19],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"2 Pet. ii. 19."},{"id":"260394f845ef","v":"npnf.augustinus.de_civitate_dei","w":"augustinus.de_civitate_dei","a":"augustinus_von_hippo","s":555,"p":[0,0],"r":[3,8],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"2 Pet. iii. 8."},{"id":"a216e8f63941","v":"npnf.augustinus.de_civitate_dei","w":"augustinus.de_civitate_dei","a":"augustinus_von_hippo","s":566,"p":[0,0],"r":[3,3,3,13],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"2 Pet. iii. 3-13. The whole passage is quoted by Augustin."},{"id":"6c8a3192c262","v":"npnf.augustinus.de_civitate_dei","w":"augustinus.de_civitate_dei","a":"augustinus_von_hippo","s":572,"p":[0,0],"r":[3,6],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"2 Pet. iii. 6."},{"id":"a10dd1b4a03c","v":"npnf.augustinus.de_civitate_dei","w":"augustinus.de_civitate_dei","a":"augustinus_von_hippo","s":572,"p":[0,0],"r":[3,10],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"2 Pet. iii. 10, 11."},{"id":"583745f7e4a6","v":"npnf.augustinus.de_civitate_dei","w":"augustinus.de_civitate_dei","a":"augustinus_von_hippo","s":602,"p":[0,0],"r":[2,4],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"2 Pet. ii. 4."},{"id":"af8e36464abe","v":"npnf.augustinus.de_trinitate","w":"augustinus.de_trinitate","a":"augustinus_von_hippo","s":38,"p":[1,1],"r":[1,4],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"[The original is: \" ut sit participatio ejus in idipsum .\" The English translator renders: \"So that it may partake thereof in itself.\" The thought of Augustin is, that the believing soul though mutable partakes of the immutable; and he designates the immutable as the in idipsum: the self-existent. In that striking passage in the Confessions, in which he describes the spiritual and extatic meditations of himself and his mother, as they looked out upon the Mediterranean from the windows at Ostia-a scene well known from Ary Schefer's painting-he denominates God the idipsum: the \"self same\" (Confessions IX. x). Augustin refers to the same absolute immutability of God, in this place. By faith, man is \"a partaker of a divine nature,\" (2 Pet. i. 4.)-W.G.T.S.]."},{"id":"b2e9cac9ccde","v":"npnf.augustinus.enchiridion","w":"augustinus.enchiridion","a":"augustinus_von_hippo","s":32,"p":[0,0],"r":[2,19],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"2 Pet. ii. 19."},{"id":"40f43d576905","v":"npnf.augustinus.enchiridion","w":"augustinus.enchiridion","a":"augustinus_von_hippo","s":59,"p":[0,0],"r":[2,4],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"2 Pet. ii. 4."},{"id":"f045bee8d308","v":"npnf.augustinus.enchiridion","w":"augustinus.enchiridion","a":"augustinus_von_hippo","s":120,"p":[0,0],"r":[2,19],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"2 Pet. ii. 19."},{"id":"63498ee97cb9","v":"npnf.augustinus.de_spiritu_et_littera","w":"augustinus.de_spiritu_et_littera","a":"augustinus_von_hippo","s":53,"p":[0,0],"r":[2,19],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"2 Pet. ii. 19."},{"id":"14a5013ce9b9","v":"npnf.augustinus.de_perfectione","w":"augustinus.de_perfectione","a":"augustinus_von_hippo","s":11,"p":[0,0],"r":[2,19],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"2 Pet. ii. 19."},{"id":"09e2c6fe790e","v":"npnf.augustinus.de_gestis_pelagii","w":"augustinus.de_gestis_pelagii","a":"augustinus_von_hippo","s":45,"p":[0,0],"r":[1,4],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"2 Pet. i. 4."},{"id":"1d559e1c2907","v":"npnf.augustinus.de_gestis_pelagii","w":"augustinus.de_gestis_pelagii","a":"augustinus_von_hippo","s":68,"p":[0,0],"r":[1,4],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"2 Pet. i. 4."},{"id":"62903060074d","v":"npnf.augustinus.de_nuptiis","w":"augustinus.de_nuptiis","a":"augustinus_von_hippo","s":51,"p":[0,0],"r":[2,19],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"2 Pet. ii. 